Non-generic version, then generic:

```go
func MapInts(arr []int, f func(int) int) []int {
    res := make([]int, len(arr))
    for i, v := range arr {
        res[i] = f(v)
    }
    return res
}

func Map[S ~[]T, T, R any](arr S, f func(T) R) []R {
    res := make([]R, len(arr))
    for i, v := range arr {
        res[i] = f(v)
    }
    return res
}

// Map([]int{1, 2, 3}, strconv.Itoa) → ["1" "2" "3"]
```

`S ~[]T` accepts named slice types too; the output type `R` can differ from the input. Preallocating with `make(len)` avoids regrowth. With Go 1.23 iterators you could also write a lazy `func Map[T, R any](seq iter.Seq[T], f func(T) R) iter.Seq[R]`.

